# Bots Structured Reference

This file reorganizes bot knowledge into the same keyed mechanic format used by other deterministic knowledge sources.
The original raw source remains preserved in public/knowledge/bots for side-by-side comparison.

Mechanic: Bots
Type: System
Domain: Event Shop
Section: Bots
Category: Medal Progression
Aliases: none.
Disambiguation: This chunk is about the Bots mechanic itself, not its interactions. It is not about individual bot stat tables, shorthand aliases alone, or tracker implementation details.
Definition: Bots are medal-based upgrades purchased in the Event Shop. Once unlocked, bot ownership and medal upgrades persist across events rather than resetting each event.
Behavior:
Bots can only be purchased with medals in the Event Shop.
Bots purchased do not reset each event.
The shop offers 4 bots: Flame Bot, Thunder Bot, Golden Bot, and Amplify Bot.
Bots can be turned off and on in the shop between rounds.
Each bot has 4 medal-upgraded stats.
Unlock Costs:
Bot unlock costs depend on how many bots have already been purchased.
1st bot: 150 medals.
2nd bot: 300 medals.
3rd bot: 600 medals.
4th bot: 900 medals.
Shared Upgrade Costs:
All bot stat upgrades use the shared medal ladder shown in the raw source overview table.
Level 1 costs 100 medals and each later level adds 40 medals.
The shared table in the raw source lists costs through level 20, ending at 860 medals for level 20.
Aliases:
Players commonly use shorthand names for bots in questions and guides.
GB and CB both refer to Golden Bot, which many players also call Coin Bot.
AB refers to Amplify Bot.
TB refers to Thunder Bot.
FB refers to Flame Bot.
Bot Respec:
Bots and their spent medals can be refunded through a bot respec.
Bot respec is available for 300 Gems once per event.
Labs completed for bots are not refunded through a bot respec; only medal-related unlocks and upgrades are refunded.

Mechanic: Flame Bot
Type: Bot
Domain: Event Shop
Section: Bots
Category: Area of Effect
Aliases: fb
Disambiguation: This chunk is about Flame Bot as an individual bot mechanic itself, not its interactions. It is not about Thunder Bot, Golden Bot, Amplify Bot, or shorthand bot aliases as a standalone topic.
Definition: Flame Bot damages enemies in an area around the bot and applies a burn effect.
Unlocking/Upgrading:
Like all bots, Flame Bot is unlocked and upgraded in the Event Shop menu.
The unlock cost depends on how many other bots have been bought.
The raw source says each of Flame Bot's upgrade rows starts from the shared 100-medal base ladder and increases by 40 medals each level.
Upgrade Stats:
Damage Reduction
Cooldown
Damage
Range
Behavior:
Flame Bot deals burn damage and does 1 tick of damage equal to bot damage per second.
Damage Reduction starts at 20%.
Cooldown starts at 75 seconds.
Damage starts at x50 tower damage.
Range starts at 30m.
Damage Reduction reduces the amount of damage burned enemies deal.
Cooldown is the time between activations.
Damage increases the damage dealt when Flame Bot activates.
Range increases the area the bot covers while active.
Labs:
Flame Bot Cooldown unlocks in Milestones at Tier 5 Wave 60 and reduces bot cooldown by 1 second per level. Has 25 levels for 25 seconds total reduction.
Flame Bot - Burn Stack unlocks in Milestones at Tier 10 Wave 50 and allows successive hits on the same enemy to stack burn and increase burn tick frequency. Has 5 levels adding 1 stack each level, with a cap of 10 stacks of burn.
Interactions:
Flame Bot damage takes into account crit and super crit factor and chance.
Flame Bot range is amplified by tower range.

Mechanic: Thunder Bot
Type: Bot
